indexContent(domain) ::= <<
# TeaQL Rust Tool API Reference

> [!WARNING]
> **DO NOT GUESS TOOL APIS.** The published surface is the versioned
> request-scoped \`teaql-tool-context\` facade. A module absent from this inventory is unsupported.

To get the exact API usage and examples for TeaQL Tool APIs, execute the following command:

```bash
cargo teaql --input models/<domain.name>.xml rust-assist-tool-api/[module]
```

Replace \`[module]\` with one of the following:

```json
{"schema":"io.teaql.assist.tool-api/v1","language":"rust","crate":"teaql-tool-context","version":"2.0.0","intent":"comment","modules":[{"name":"time","feature":"std","facade":"context.time()"},{"name":"id","feature":"std","facade":"context.id()"},{"name":"text","feature":"std","facade":"context.text()"},{"name":"json","feature":"std","facade":"context.json()"},{"name":"decimal","feature":"std","facade":"context.decimal()"},{"name":"money","feature":"std","facade":"context.money()"},{"name":"http","feature":"http","facade":"context.http()"}]}
```

| module | Facade | Feature | Native result |
|---|---|---|---|
| time | \`context.time()\` | \`std\` | chrono value behind \`.comment(...)\` |
| id | \`context.id()\` | \`std\` | \`String\` behind \`.comment(...)\` |
| text | \`context.text()\` | \`std\` | \`String\` / \`bool\` behind \`.comment(...)\` |
| json | \`context.json()\` | \`std\` | serde JSON / result, selected reads require comment |
| decimal | \`context.decimal()\` | \`std\` | decimal / result behind \`.comment(...)\` |
| money | \`context.money()\` | \`std\` | money / result behind \`.comment(...)\` |
| http | \`context.http()\` | \`http\` | awaitable \`Result\<String, String\>\` after comment |

The inventory intentionally contains only modules exercised by the conformance gate. Fetch
one module for its exact signatures. Unknown modules are rejected with HTTP 404.

Once the command succeeds, read its output. Use the printed code as a template to write your logic.
>>
